{number: 100}
{title: Sweet Hour of Prayer}
{key: C}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[C] Sweet hour of prayer, sweet [F] hour of prayer,
That [C] calls me from a [G7] world of care,
And [C] bids me at my [F] Father's throne,
Make [C] all my wants and [G7] wishes [C] known!
In [C] seasons of dis-[F] tress and grief,
My [C] soul has often [G7] found relief,
And [C] oft escaped the [F] tempter's snare,
By [C] thy return, sweet [G7] hour of [C] prayer.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 2}
[C] Sweet hour of prayer, sweet [F] hour of prayer,
The [C] joys I feel, the [G7] bliss I share
Of [C] those whose anxious [F] spirits burn
With [C] strong desires for [G7] thy re-[C] turn!
With [C] such I hasten [F] to the place
Where [C] God, my Saviour, [G7] shows His face,
And [C] gladly take my [F] station there,
And [C] wait for thee, sweet [G7] hour of [C] prayer.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
[C] Sweet hour of prayer, sweet [F] hour of prayer,
Thy [C] wings shall my pe-[G7] tition bear
To [C] Him, whose truth and [F] faithfulness
En-[C] gage the waiting the [G7] soul to [C] bless:
And [C] since He bids me [F] seek His face,
Be-[C] lieve His Word, and [G7] trust His grace,
I'll [C] cast on Him my [F] ev'ry care,
And [C] wait for thee, sweet [G7] hour of [C] prayer.
{end_of_verse}
